From: XR1710G Maintainer <maintainer@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: bridge: retain VLAN context for forward output

After mapping an access-port PVID to the bridge VLAN device on ingress,
bridge netfilter must present the same VLAN device as the forward hook
egress context. Otherwise firewall4 sees the bridge master as the output
device and zone egress matching rejects valid bridged traffic.

Restrict this to bridges with VLAN filtering enabled. Non-VLAN-aware
bridges retain the upstream bridge-master output device.

Signed-off-by: XR1710G Maintainer <maintainer@example.com>
---
 net/bridge/br_netfilter_hooks.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/net/bridge/br_netfilter_hooks.c
+++ b/net/bridge/br_netfilter_hooks.c
@@ -702,5 +702,8 @@ static unsigned int br_nf_forward_ip(struct sk_buff *skb,
 	parent = bridge_parent(state->out);
 	if (!parent)
 		return NF_DROP_REASON(skb, SKB_DROP_REASON_DEV_READY, 0);
 
+	if (br_opt_get(netdev_priv(parent), BROPT_VLAN_ENABLED))
+		parent = brnf_get_logical_dev(skb, state->in, state->net);
+
 	nf_bridge_pull_encap_header(skb);
